{"id":"mahabharata-7-069","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":69,"title":"एकोनसप्ततितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 69 · Drona arms Duryodhana","summary":{"en":"Arjuna presses on, and Duryodhana tells Drona that Arjuna has passed him. Drona binds a magical armour on Duryodhana by incantation and sends him against Arjuna.","kn":"ಅರ್ಜುನ ಮುನ್ನುಗ್ಗುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅರ್ಜುನ ತನ್ನನ್ನು ದಾಟಿದನೆಂದು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನ ದ್ರೋಣನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ದ್ರೋಣ ಮಂತ್ರದಿಂದ ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನಿಗೆ ದಿವ್ಯ ಕವಚ ಕಟ್ಟಿ ಅರ್ಜುನನ ವಿರುದ್ಧ ಕಳುಹಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अर्जुन आगे बढ़ते हैं और दुर्योधन द्रोण से कहता है कि अर्जुन उनसे आगे निकल गया। द्रोण मन्त्र से दुर्योधन को दिव्य कवच बाँधकर उसे अर्जुन के विरुद्ध भेजते हैं।","te":"అర్జునుడు ముందుకు సాగగా అతడు తనను దాటిపోయాడని దుర్యోధనుడు ద్రోణునికి చెబుతాడు. ద్రోణుడు మంత్రంతో దుర్యోధనునికి దివ్య కవచాన్ని కట్టి అర్జునునిపైకి పంపుతాడు.","ta":"அர்ஜுனன் முன்னேற, அவன் தன்னைக் கடந்துவிட்டான் என்று துரியோதனன் த்ரோணரிடம் கூறுகிறான். த்ரோணர் மந்திரத்தால் துரியோதனனுக்குத் தெய்வீகக் கவசம் கட்டி அர்ஜுனனுக்கு எதிராக அனுப்புகிறார்.","ml":"അർജുനൻ മുന്നോട്ടു പോകുന്നുവെന്ന് ദുര്യോധനൻ ദ്രോണരോട് പറയുന്നു. മന്ത്രം ചൊല്ലി ദ്രോണർ ദുര്യോധനന് മായാകവചം കെട്ടി അർജുനനെതിരെ അയയ്ക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.69; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"जयद्रथवधपर्व","titleEn":"Jayadrathavadha Parva (Slaying of Jayadratha)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः प्रविष्टे कौन्तेये सिन्धुराजजिघांसया ।\nद्रोणानीकं विनिर्भिद्य भोजानीकं च दुस्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, after Arjuna had entered, intent on killing the king of the Sindhus, breaking through Drona's division and the hard-to-cross division of the Bhojas,"}},{"n":2,"text":"काम्बोजस्य च दायादे हते राजन्सुदक्षिणे ।\nश्रुतायुधे च विक्रान्ते निहते सव्यसाचिना ॥","meaning":{"en":"after Sudakshina, heir of the Kamboja, was slain, O king, and the valiant Shrutayudha killed by the left-handed archer,"}},{"n":3,"text":"विप्रद्रुतेष्वनीकेषु विध्वस्तेषु समन्ततः ।\nप्रभग्नं स्वबलं दृष्ट्वा पुत्रस्ते द्रोणमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"when the divisions had fled and been shattered everywhere, your son, seeing his own force broken, went to Drona."}},{"n":4,"text":"त्वरन्नेकरथेनैव समेत्य द्रोणमब्रवीत् ।\nगतः स पुरुषव्याघ्रः प्रमथ्येमां महाचमूम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming up quickly in a single chariot, he said to Drona: That tiger among men has gone on, having ploughed through this great army."}},{"n":5,"text":"अत्र बुद्ध्या समीक्षस्व किं नु कार्यमनन्तरम् ।\nअर्जुनस्य विघाताय दारुणेऽस्मिञ्जनक्षये ॥","meaning":{"en":"Consider with your judgement what should be done next to stop Arjuna in this dreadful slaughter of men."}},{"n":6,"text":"यथा स पुरुषव्याघ्रो न हन्येत जयद्रथः ।\nतथा विधत्स्व भद्रं ते त्वं हि नः परमा गतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Arrange it so that the tiger among men, Jayadratha, is not killed. May good come to you; you are our final refuge."}},{"n":7,"text":"असौ धनंजयाग्निर्हि कोपमारुतचोदितः ।\nसेनाकक्षं दहति मे वह्निः कक्षमिवोत्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"That fire, Dhananjaya, driven by the wind of his anger, is burning my army as a fire that has risen burns dry grass."}},{"n":8,"text":"अतिक्रान्ते हि कौन्तेये भित्त्वा सैन्यं परंतप ।\nजयद्रथस्य गोप्तारः संशयं परमं गताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Now that Kunti's son has broken the army and passed on, O scourge of foes, Jayadratha's protectors are in grave danger."}},{"n":9,"text":"स्थिरा बुद्धिर्नरेन्द्राणामासीद्ब्रह्मविदां वर ।\nनातिक्रमिष्यति द्रोणं जातु जीवन्धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of the Brahma-knowing, the kings were firmly convinced that Dhananjaya would never get past Drona while alive."}},{"n":10,"text":"सोऽसौ पार्थो व्यतिक्रान्तो मिषतस्ते महाद्युते ।\nसर्वं ह्यद्यातुरं मन्ये नैतदस्ति बलं मम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet that Partha has gone past, radiant one, before your very eyes. I think all is distressed now; this strength of mine is nothing."}},{"n":11,"text":"जानामि त्वां महाभाग पाण्डवानां हिते रतम् ।\nतथा मुह्यामि च ब्रह्मन्कार्यवत्तां विचिन्तयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know, great sir, that you are devoted to the good of the Pandavas, and so I am confused, brahmana, as I think about what is to be done."}},{"n":12,"text":"यथाशक्ति च ते ब्रह्मन्वर्तये वृत्तिमुत्तमाम् ।\nप्रीणामि च यथाशक्ति तच्च त्वं नावबुध्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I serve you, brahmana, with the best livelihood as far as I can, and please you as far as I can; but you do not understand it."}},{"n":13,"text":"अस्मान्न त्वं सदा भक्तानिच्छस्यमितविक्रम ।\nपाण्डवान्सततं प्रीणास्यस्माकं विप्रिये रतान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"You, of measureless valour, do not wish for us who are always devoted; you ever please the Pandavas, who delight in our harm."}},{"n":14,"text":"अस्मानेवोपजीवंस्त्वमस्माकं विप्रिये रतः ।\nन ह्यहं त्वां विजानामि मधुदिग्धमिव क्षुरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Living off us, you delight in what harms us. I did not know you, like a razor smeared with honey."}},{"n":15,"text":"नादास्यच्चेद्वरं मह्यं भवान्पाण्डवनिग्रहे ।\nनावारयिष्यं गच्छन्तमहं सिन्धुपतिं गृहान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you had not given me the boon of restraining the Pandavas, I would not have stopped the king of the Sindhus when he wished to go home."}},{"n":16,"text":"मया त्वाशंसमानेन त्वत्तस्त्राणमबुद्धिना ।\nआश्वासितः सिन्धुपतिर्मोहाद्दत्तश्च मृत्यवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I, hoping for protection from you, in my foolishness comforted the king of the Sindhus and so delivered him to death."}},{"n":17,"text":"यमदंष्ट्रान्तरं प्राप्तो मुच्येतापि हि मानवः ।\nनार्जुनस्य वशं प्राप्तो मुच्येताजौ जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who has got between the teeth of Yama may be freed, but Jayadratha, fallen into Arjuna's power in battle, will not be."}},{"n":18,"text":"स तथा कुरु शोणाश्व यथा रक्ष्येत सैन्धवः ।\nमम चार्तप्रलापानां मा क्रुधः पाहि सैन्धवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"So act, lord of the red horses, so that the Saindhava is guarded. Do not be angry at my pained words; protect the Saindhava."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":19,"text":"नाभ्यसूयामि ते वाचमश्वत्थाम्नासि मे समः ।\nसत्यं तु ते प्रवक्ष्यामि तज्जुषस्व विशां पते ॥","meaning":{"en":"I take no offence at your words; you are equal to me as Ashvatthama is. But I will tell you the truth; accept it, lord of men."}},{"n":20,"text":"सारथिः प्रवरः कृष्णः शीघ्राश्चास्य हयोत्तमाः ।\nअल्पं च विवरं कृत्वा तूर्णं याति धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krishna is the best of charioteers, his horses are the finest and swift, and Dhananjaya, going through even a small gap, passes quickly."}},{"n":21,"text":"किं नु पश्यसि बाणौघान्क्रोशमात्रे किरीटिनः ।\nपश्चाद्रथस्य पतितान्क्षिप्ताञ्शीघ्रं हि गच्छतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Do you not see the floods of arrows fallen a krosha behind the diademed Arjuna's chariot, shot as he speeds on?"}},{"n":22,"text":"न चाहं शीघ्रयानेऽद्य समर्थो वयसान्वितः ।\nसेनामुखे च पार्थानामेतद्बलमुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"And I, burdened with age, am not able today to move fast; and the Pandava force stands here at the front of the army."}},{"n":23,"text":"युधिष्ठिरश्च मे ग्राह्यो मिषतां सर्वधन्विनाम् ।\nएवं मया प्रतिज्ञातं क्षत्रमध्ये महाभुज ॥","meaning":{"en":"Moreover, mighty-armed, I have vowed in the midst of the kshatriyas that I will seize Yudhishthira before the eyes of all bowmen."}},{"n":24,"text":"धनंजयेन चोत्सृष्टो वर्तते प्रमुखे मम ।\nतस्माद्व्यूहमुखं हित्वा नाहं यास्यामि फल्गुनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhananjaya has left him, and he is right before me. So I will not leave the front of the formation and go after Phalguna."}},{"n":25,"text":"तुल्याभिजनकर्माणं शत्रुमेकं सहायवान् ।\nगत्वा योधय मा भैस्त्वं त्वं ह्यस्य जगतः पतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Go yourself, with allies, and fight this one enemy who is your equal in birth and deeds; do not be afraid, for you are lord of this world."}},{"n":26,"text":"राजा शूरः कृती दक्षो वैरमुत्पाद्य पाण्डवैः ।\nवीर स्वयं प्रयाह्याशु यत्र यातो धनंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, you are brave, accomplished and skilled, and you started this feud with the Pandavas; so, hero, go quickly yourself to where Dhananjaya has gone."}},{"text":"दुर्योधन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Duryodhana said:"}},{"n":27,"text":"कथं त्वामप्यतिक्रान्तः सर्वशस्त्रभृतां वरः ।\nधनंजयो मया शक्य आचार्य प्रतिबाधितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Teacher, how can I check Dhananjaya, best of all weapon-bearers, who has even passed you?"}},{"n":28,"text":"अपि शक्यो रणे जेतुं वज्रहस्तः पुरंदरः ।\nनार्जुनः समरे शक्यो जेतुं परपुरंजयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even Purandara, thunderbolt in hand, might be conquered in battle, but not Arjuna, conqueror of enemy cities."}},{"n":29,"text":"येन भोजश्च हार्दिक्यो भवांश्च त्रिदशोपमः ।\nअस्त्रप्रतापेन जितौ श्रुतायुश्च निबर्हितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By the power of his weapons he has defeated the Bhoja, Hridika's son, and you, who are like the gods, and he has killed Shrutayu."}},{"n":30,"text":"सुदक्षिणश्च निहतः स च राजा श्रुतायुधः ।\nश्रुतायुश्चाच्युतायुश्च म्लेच्छाश्च शतशो हताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sudakshina and King Shrutayudha are slain, and Shrutayu and Achyutayu, and barbarians by hundreds."}},{"n":31,"text":"तं कथं पाण्डवं युद्धे दहन्तमहितान्बहून् ।\nप्रतियोत्स्यामि दुर्धर्षं तन्मे शंसास्त्रकोविद ॥","meaning":{"en":"How shall I face that unassailable Pandava in battle, as he burns many foes? Tell me, you who know weapons."}},{"n":32,"text":"क्षमं चेन्मन्यसे युद्धं मम तेनाद्य शाधि माम् ।\nपरवानस्मि भवति प्रेष्यकृद्रक्ष मे यशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you think battle with him is fitting for me today, instruct me. I am dependent on you, a servant; guard my fame."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":33,"text":"सत्यं वदसि कौरव्य दुराधर्षो धनंजयः ।\nअहं तु तत्करिष्यामि यथैनं प्रसहिष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You speak truly, Kaurava: Dhananjaya is hard to assail. But I will do such a thing that you will be able to withstand him."}},{"n":34,"text":"अद्भुतं चाद्य पश्यन्तु लोके सर्वधनुर्धराः ।\nविषक्तं त्वयि कौन्तेयं वासुदेवस्य पश्यतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Today let all the world's bowmen see a wonder: the son of Kunti engaged with you, while Vasudeva looks on."}},{"n":35,"text":"एष ते कवचं राजंस्तथा बध्नामि काञ्चनम् ।\nयथा न बाणा नास्त्राणि विषहिष्यन्ति ते रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, I now bind on you this golden armour in such a way that neither arrows nor weapons will pierce you in battle."}},{"n":36,"text":"यदि त्वां सासुरसुराः सयक्षोरगराक्षसाः ।\nयोधयन्ति त्रयो लोकाः सनरा नास्ति ते भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Even if the three worlds with asuras and gods, yakshas, serpents, rakshasas and men fight you, you have no fear."}},{"n":37,"text":"न कृष्णो न च कौन्तेयो न चान्यः शस्त्रभृद्रणे ।\nशरानर्पयितुं कश्चित्कवचे तव शक्ष्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Neither Krishna nor Kunti's son nor any other weapon-bearer in battle will be able to send arrows into your armour."}},{"n":38,"text":"स त्वं कवचमास्थाय क्रुद्धमद्य रणेऽर्जुनम् ।\nत्वरमाणः स्वयं याहि न चासौ त्वां सहिष्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"So, in this armour, go yourself quickly against the angry Arjuna in battle; he will not be able to withstand you."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":39,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा त्वरन्द्रोणः स्पृष्ट्वाम्भो वर्म भास्वरम् ।\nआबबन्धाद्भुततमं जपन्मन्त्रं यथाविधि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, Drona quickly touched water and, reciting a mantra according to rule, bound on the radiant, wondrous armour,"}},{"n":40,"text":"रणे तस्मिन्सुमहति विजयाय सुतस्य ते ।\nविसिस्मापयिषुर्लोकं विद्यया ब्रह्मवित्तमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"for the victory of your son in that great battle, the best of Brahma-knowers wishing to astonish the world by his science."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":41,"text":"करोतु स्वस्ति ते ब्रह्मा स्वस्ति चापि द्विजातयः ।\nसरीसृपाश्च ये श्रेष्ठास्तेभ्यस्ते स्वस्ति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"May Brahma grant you well-being, and the twice-born too. May those who are the foremost of the reptiles grant you well-being, Bharata."}},{"n":42,"text":"ययातिर्नहुषश्चैव धुन्धुमारो भगीरथः ।\nतुभ्यं राजर्षयः सर्वे स्वस्ति कुर्वन्तु सर्वशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"May Yayati, Nahusha, Dhundhumara and Bhagiratha, all the royal sages, bring you well-being on every side."}},{"n":43,"text":"स्वस्ति तेऽस्त्वेकपादेभ्यो बहुपादेभ्य एव च ।\nस्वस्त्यस्त्वपादकेभ्यश्च नित्यं तव महारणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"May you have well-being from creatures with one foot and many feet, and may creatures with none always bless you in the great battle."}},{"n":44,"text":"स्वाहा स्वधा शची चैव स्वस्ति कुर्वन्तु ते सदा ।\nलक्ष्मीररुन्धती चैव कुरुतां स्वस्ति तेऽनघ ॥","meaning":{"en":"May Svaha, Svadha and Shachi always grant you well-being; may Lakshmi and Arundhati make it well for you, sinless one."}},{"n":45,"text":"असितो देवलश्चैव विश्वामित्रस्तथाङ्गिराः ।\nवसिष्ठः कश्यपश्चैव स्वस्ति कुर्वन्तु ते नृप ॥","meaning":{"en":"May Asita, Devala, Vishvamitra, Angiras, Vasishtha and Kashyapa bring you well-being, king."}},{"n":46,"text":"धाता विधाता लोकेशो दिशश्च सदिगीश्वराः ।\nस्वस्ति तेऽद्य प्रयच्छन्तु कार्त्तिकेयश्च षण्मुखः ॥","meaning":{"en":"May Dhatri, Vidhatri, the lord of the worlds, the quarters with their regents, and six-faced Kartikeya grant you well-being today."}},{"n":47,"text":"विवस्वान्भगवान्स्वस्ति करोतु तव सर्वशः ।\nदिग्गजाश्चैव चत्वारः क्षितिः खं गगनं ग्रहाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"May the blessed Vivasvan bring you well-being in every way; the four elephants of the quarters, earth, space, sky and the planets too."}},{"n":48,"text":"अधस्ताद्धरणीं योऽसौ सदा धारयते नृप ।\nस शेषः पन्नगश्रेष्ठः स्वस्ति तुभ्यं प्रयच्छतु ॥","meaning":{"en":"May Shesha, best of serpents, who always bears the earth beneath, grant you well-being, king."}},{"n":49,"text":"गान्धारे युधि विक्रम्य निर्जिताः सुरसत्तमाः ।\nपुरा वृत्रेण दैत्येन भिन्नदेहाः सहस्रशः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Son of Gandhari, long ago the best of the gods, having fought in battle, were defeated by the demon Vritra, thousands of them with bodies torn."}},{"n":50,"text":"हृततेजोबलाः सर्वे तदा सेन्द्रा दिवौकसः ।\nब्रह्माणं शरणं जग्मुर्वृत्राद्भीता महासुरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the dwellers in heaven with Indra, their strength and splendour taken, afraid of the great asura Vritra, went to Brahma for shelter."}},{"text":"देवा ऊचुः","meaning":{"en":"The gods said:"}},{"n":51,"text":"प्रमर्दितानां वृत्रेण देवानां देवसत्तम ।\nगतिर्भव सुरश्रेष्ठ त्राहि नो महतो भयात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Best of gods, be the refuge of the gods crushed by Vritra; best of the deities, save us from great fear."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":52,"text":"अथ पार्श्वे स्थितं विष्णुं शक्रादींश्च सुरोत्तमान् ।\nप्राह तथ्यमिदं वाक्यं विषण्णान्सुरसत्तमान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Brahma spoke these true words to Vishnu standing at his side and to Shakra and the other foremost gods, who were despondent."}},{"n":53,"text":"रक्ष्या मे सततं देवाः सहेन्द्राः सद्विजातयः ।\nत्वष्टुः सुदुर्धरं तेजो येन वृत्रो विनिर्मितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Brahma said: The gods with Indra and the twice-born are always to be protected by me. But Tvashtri's splendour, with which Vritra was made, is very hard to bear."}},{"n":54,"text":"त्वष्ट्रा पुरा तपस्तप्त्वा वर्षायुतशतं तदा ।\nवृत्रो विनिर्मितो देवाः प्राप्यानुज्ञां महेश्वरात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Long ago, O gods, Tvashtri, after practising austerity for a million years, made Vritra, having gained leave from Maheshvara."}},{"n":55,"text":"स तस्यैव प्रसादाद्वै हन्यादेव रिपुर्बली ।\nनागत्वा शंकरस्थानं भगवान्दृश्यते हरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By that same god's grace the strong enemy might be killed; but the blessed Hara is not seen without going to Shankara's abode."}},{"n":56,"text":"दृष्ट्वा हनिष्यथ रिपुं क्षिप्रं गच्छत मन्दरम् ।\nयत्रास्ते तपसां योनिर्दक्षयज्ञविनाशनः ।\nपिनाकी सर्वभूतेशो भगनेत्रनिपातनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing him you will quickly kill your enemy. Go to Mandara, where he is, the source of austerities, the destroyer of Daksha's sacrifice, the bearer of the Pinaka, lord of all beings, who struck out Bhaga's eyes."}},{"n":57,"text":"ते गत्वा सहिता देवा ब्रह्मणा सह मन्दरम् ।\nअपश्यंस्तेजसां राशिं सूर्यकोटिसमप्रभम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The gods, together with Brahma, went to Mandara and saw a mass of splendour, bright as ten million suns."}},{"n":58,"text":"सोऽब्रवीत्स्वागतं देवा ब्रूत किं करवाण्यहम् ।\nअमोघं दर्शनं मह्यं कामप्राप्तिरतोऽस्तु वः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He said: Welcome, gods. Tell me what I may do. Seeing me is never in vain; therefore let your wishes be fulfilled."}},{"n":59,"text":"एवमुक्तास्तु ते सर्वे प्रत्यूचुस्तं दिवौकसः ।\nतेजो हृतं नो वृत्रेण गतिर्भव दिवौकसाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, all those dwellers in heaven answered him: Vritra has taken away our splendour. Be the refuge of the heaven-dwellers."}},{"n":60,"text":"मूर्तीरीक्षष्व नो देव प्रहारैर्जर्जरीकृताः ।\nशरणं त्वां प्रपन्नाः स्म गतिर्भव महेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Look on our bodies, god, shattered by blows. We have come to you for shelter; be our refuge, Maheshvara."}},{"text":"महेश्वर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Maheshvara said:"}},{"n":61,"text":"विदितं मे यथा देवाः कृत्येयं सुमहाबला ।\nत्वष्टुस्तेजोभवा घोरा दुर्निवार्याकृतात्मभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"I know, gods, how mighty this fell power is, born of Tvashtri's splendour, impossible to restrain for those of unschooled selves."}},{"n":62,"text":"अवश्यं तु मया कार्यं साह्यं सर्वदिवौकसाम् ।\nममेदं गात्रजं शक्र कवचं गृह्य भास्वरम् ।\nबधानानेन मन्त्रेण मानसेन सुरेश्वर ॥","meaning":{"en":"But I must certainly help all the heaven-dwellers. Shakra, take this shining armour that has come from my own body, and bind it on, lord of gods, with this mantra, in the mind."}},{"text":"द्रोण उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Drona said:"}},{"n":63,"text":"इत्युक्त्वा वरदः प्रादाद्वर्म तन्मन्त्रमेव च ।\nस तेन वर्मणा गुप्तः प्रायाद्वृत्रचमूं प्रति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this, the giver of boons gave the armour and the mantra too. Protected by that armour, Indra advanced against Vritra's army."}},{"n":64,"text":"नानाविधैश्च शस्त्रौघैः पात्यमानैर्महारणे ।\nन संधिः शक्यते भेत्तुं वर्मबन्धस्य तस्य तु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Though showers of many kinds of weapons were hurled in the great battle, the joint of that armour's binding could not be broken."}},{"n":65,"text":"ततो जघान समरे वृत्रं देवपतिः स्वयम् ।\nतं च मन्त्रमयं बन्धं वर्म चाङ्गिरसे ददौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the lord of the gods himself killed Vritra in battle, and gave that mantra-made binding and the armour to Angiras."}},{"n":66,"text":"अङ्गिराः प्राह पुत्रस्य मन्त्रज्ञस्य बृहस्पतेः ।\nबृहस्पतिरथोवाच अग्निवेश्याय धीमते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Angiras gave it to his son Brihaspati, who knew the mantra; and Brihaspati then gave it to the wise Agnivesya."}},{"n":67,"text":"अग्निवेश्यो मम प्रादात्तेन बध्नामि वर्म ते ।\nतवाद्य देहरक्षार्थं मन्त्रेण नृपसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agnivesya gave it to me; with it I bind armour on you today, best of kings, with the mantra, to guard your body."}},{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":68,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा ततो द्रोणस्तव पुत्रं महाद्युतिः ।\nपुनरेव वचः प्राह शनैराचार्यपुंगवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to your son, the radiant Drona, best of teachers, again spoke slowly."}},{"n":69,"text":"ब्रह्मसूत्रेण बध्नामि कवचं तव पार्थिव ।\nहिरण्यगर्भेण यथा बद्धं विष्णोः पुरा रणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"I bind your armour with the Brahma-thread, king, as Hiranyagarbha bound it for Vishnu in a battle long ago."}},{"n":70,"text":"यथा च ब्रह्मणा बद्धं संग्रामे तारकामये ।\nशक्रस्य कवचं दिव्यं तथा बध्नाम्यहं तव ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Brahma bound Indra's divine armour in the war on account of Taraka, so I bind yours."}},{"n":71,"text":"बद्ध्वा तु कवचं तस्य मन्त्रेण विधिपूर्वकम् ।\nप्रेषयामास राजानं युद्धाय महते द्विजः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bound the king's armour with the mantra, according to rule, the brahmana sent him to the great battle."}},{"n":72,"text":"स संनद्धो महाबाहुराचार्येण महात्मना ।\nरथानां च सहस्रेण त्रिगर्तानां प्रहारिणाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Armoured by the great-souled teacher, the mighty-armed Duryodhana set out with a thousand chariots of the Trigarta fighters,"}},{"n":73,"text":"तथा दन्तिसहस्रेण मत्तानां वीर्यशालिनाम् ।\nअश्वानामयुतेनैव तथान्यैश्च महारथैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"a thousand strong and maddened elephants, ten thousand horses, and other great chariot-warriors,"}},{"n":74,"text":"वृतः प्रायान्महाबाहुरर्जुनस्य रथं प्रति ।\nनानावादित्रघोषेण यथा वैरोचनिस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"and, surrounded by them, advanced toward Arjuna's chariot with the din of many instruments, like Bali, son of Virochana."}},{"n":75,"text":"ततः शब्दो महानासीत्सैन्यानां तव भारत ।\nअगाधं प्रस्थितं दृष्ट्वा समुद्रमिव कौरवम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, O Bharata, a great noise rose from your armies, seeing the Kaurava host move on like a fathomless sea."}}]}]}